    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the undisputed centerpiece of the lineup, commanding an elite 83.29 efficiency score. Despite facing Jack Flaherty, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a 14% platoon edge, effectively neutralizing the opponent's arm and solidifying his status as our primary producer. Complementing him are **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (62.64) and **Josh Jung** (63.73), both of whom capitalize on favorable situational factors; **Josh Jung** in particular sees a 19% boost from a soft matchup against Grayson Rodriguez (5.91 xERA). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects strongly at 60.24, acting as a high-floor anchor for our middle infield as he continues his consistent start to the 2026 campaign.\n\nOur outfield strategy remains aggressive despite some high-end pitching threats, most notably with **Josh Lowe** (48.71) and **Kyle Tucker** (52.99) drawing tough assignments against Jacob deGrom and Logan Henderson. While those matchups force a dip in their SP skill metrics, both remain rostered to capitalize on their dynamic speed and platoon profiles. The most difficult decision for today\u2019s construction was the exclusion of **Andy Pages** (45.29). Despite a respectable score, he was narrowly edged out by the superior park and platoon efficiency offered by **Dominic Smith** (59.96) and **Gage Workman** (57.41), both of whom provide better leverage in their respective spots.\n\nRisks remain elevated across the board due to the \"Lineup Pending\" status for almost every player, which forces us to rely on projected orders. We are monitoring **Liam Hicks** (55.24) and **Coby Mayo** (49.83) closely; if their actual lineup positions shift downward, their efficiency scores will adjust accordingly. Furthermore, the presence of elite arms like deGrom necessitates a disciplined approach to our game caps. While **Nasim Nunez** (50.40) provides necessary speed for our SB-starved rotation, the overall volatility of today\u2019s pitcher matchups means that any late-breaking weather updates or lineup shuffling could necessitate a quick pivot among our fringe starters to protect our seasonal volume.",
